# Port Plan — Step 07: The Run DSL (Ruby → Python)

Port `Boukensha.run` — the single entry point that wires Config, Context,
Registry, backend, PromptBuilder, Client, Logger and Agent together — plus the
tiny `RunDSL` block object that registers tools inside it.

This is the eighth of thirteen steps (`00_config` → `12_context`).

> **`run_dsl.rb` is 13 lines. That is not the step.** The step is the ~80-line
> `Boukensha.run` added to `lib/boukensha.rb`, which collapses the 92-line
> example down to 34. Budget accordingly.

> ⚠️ **Step 07 is not a linear continuation of step 06.** Three things step 06
> *deleted* are back, in their pre-06 form: `LoopError`, `Config`'s four `mud_*`
> readers, and `context.rb`'s misaligned assignments. `07/errors.rb` is
> byte-identical to `05/errors.rb`, and `07/config.rb` restores the four-line
> `mud_*` bodies that step 05 had rewritten as endless methods — while also
> reverting step 06's `@dir =` alignment and its one-line `load_env` guard. The
> evidence says step 07 was branched from around step 04/05 rather than from
> step 06. **Mirror it anyway** (standing rule: never edit the Ruby), but see
> **OQ 4** — this changes what "surface parity" is worth.

